From 51eeed65e2a4128af1f5b2673c5bca1063ac2859 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:03:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(pricing): occupancy precedence v2 - rule origin and
 infant bands rank first (G-30, G-31)

Pure pricing half of "occupancy precedence v2" (ADR-042):

- inherit.py (new, pure): PolicyLayer / cascade. Every applicable pricing
  policy contributes its rules, stamped with their origin (global 0,
  hotel 1, market 2, hotel+market 3 -> GLOBAL/HOTEL/MARKET/MARKET and
  source policy:<id>/r<rev>/<scope>). Age bands are replaced, not merged:
  the version's, else the most specific policy's. Two policies of one
  scope raise PolicyAmbiguous (a PricingError).
- model: OccupancyRule.scope_weight, ContractTerms.occupancy_precedence.
- occupancy.specificity: v2 ranks (infant slot: rule naming the infant's
  band) > origin (version > H+M > M > H > global) > level > qualifiers >
  slot. LEGACY (1) is exactly the old tuple.
- serialize: scope_weight per rule and settings.occupancy_precedence; a
  payload without the key loads as 1 and keeps its sold price.
- validate: static OCC_AMBIGUOUS error (equal rank, rules can meet in a
  sellable room/party, different values); sweep ambiguity is an ERROR;
  inherited rules for a band/room/period the contract lacks only warn
  (OCC_INHERITED_*_UNUSED); OCC_INFANT_GENERIC and NO_AGE_BANDS warnings;
  scope_weight in the duplicate signature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
