Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(commercial): every live pricing policy cascades into
 a contract; one per scope (G-30, G-31)

- contracts: _policy_for (one policy, hotel beat market) is replaced by
  _policy_layers: every policy live at the version's effective time for
  the hotel/market (global, hotel, market, hotel+market) becomes a layer;
  build_terms merges them with inherit.cascade and freezes
  occupancy_precedence=2. Two policies of one scope fail the build
  (PRICING_POLICY_AMBIGUOUS): publish refuses, validate reports BUILD.
  _bands is public as age_bands_of.
- revisions.live_or_scheduled_roots: a None filter matches a blank field
  (as as_of does) - a global scope never matched before; optional locking
  read.
- TEX Pricing Policy controller: band codes upper-cased and checked with
  ages.validate_bands; rules may not name a stay period; a room type must
  belong to the policy's hotel; activating a second live/scheduled policy
  of the same (hotel, market) is refused under a locking read.
- fixtures.create_contract(age_bands=None, occupancy_rules=None).
- test_pricing_policies (new, in CI): cascade prices and payload origins,
  market beats hotel, one policy per scope (incl. global), row checks,
  policy change reaches a contract only on republish (simulator as of the
  sale time), infant in a 2A+2C family room is free, ambiguous rules
  block publish.

