From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:13:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] fix(pricing): occupancy ties block publishing only where
 they decide a price (review of ADR-042)

- OCC_AMBIGUOUS walks the slots two tied rules share and skips one that a
  higher-ranked rule prices (an exact 2+2 rule, or the contract's own rule over a
  policy tie), a child filling an included ROOM-basis place, and a slot the runtime
  never reaches (a child before it has no rule). Findings 1 and 5.
- A pricing policy reaches every contract of its scope: inherited twins are judged
  by the same test, an inherited adult rule with a band only warns
  (OCC_INHERITED_ADULT_BAND_UNUSED); validate.policy_issues checks one policy on its
  own (adult band, combination qualifier, twins, ties in any party). Finding 2.
- OCC_POLICY_OVERRIDE_OUTRANKED warns where a policy "specific override" now loses
  to a contract rule, a more specific policy or an infant-band rule. Finding 7.
- precedence_report prices children at the start of every band of either side (a
  version frozen without bands shows its child cells) and reports rebuilds the
  publish check refuses (republish_errors). Finding 3 (pure part).
- occupancy.qualifiers_match / slot_matches shared by the runtime and the checks.

Fuzz: 4,200 random rule sets (PERSON/ROOM, fill on/off, infants counted or not):
static check and runtime agree exactly; legacy and v2 runtime unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149nHJ5M51Xm27TVWcsYSQB
