From 6623dad3257dd6dd1692374760c14a5385823cda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:13:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fix(commercial): a pricing policy is checked on its own;
 activations run one at a time

- Controller: an adult rule naming a band and a combination rule without a
  combination are refused on save; twin rules and rules that tie in some party
  (validate.policy_issues) are refused on activation. Finding 2.
- revisions.activate serialises pricing-policy activations (the DocType's own row,
  locked before Document.save locks the draft's row): two activations at once wait
  for each other instead of deadlocking in the locking scope check. Finding 6.
- policies.pricing_policy_bands: the band codes of the live policies a policy
  cascades with (price.view_cost at the hotel; other hotels' policies left out), for
  the policy editor's band picker. Finding 4 (API).
- precedence_report.run rebuilds a scheduled version as of its start, lists versions
  whose republish the publish check refuses, and scopes with a second policy live or
  scheduled. Finding 3.
- contracts.occupancy_rules_of (was _occ_rules) is public for the controller.

