From 9b371ac20da75e83beebfad862c925aeb7cbf433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:13:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(rates): a pricing policy can name the bands of the
 policies it cascades with

- The band picker of a policy rule lists the policy's own bands, then those of the
  live policies it cascades with ("CHB (from PP DE)"), so a hotel (+ market) policy
  without bands can name the market's CHB. Finding 4.
- "Specific override" on a policy rule says it ranks within that policy only.
  Finding 7 (UI).
- rates.policy.pricing.intro states the cascade: policy rules price what the
  contract's own rules leave open; policy bands only when it has none. Finding 8.
- New keys rates.policy.pricing.band_from / override_help in en, tr, de, ru, ro, pl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0149nHJ5M51Xm27TVWcsYSQB
